  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "3iLqY/ptKcSAIOKoAerGQ20mKsQ=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:29:45.691Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The spec's security section is one of the few written threat models in the repository, and its two scenarios are worth knowing because they follow from the shared-database goal.\n\n**Compromised processor instance.** A processor could access sensitive document data from the relational database, **modify database schema through migration injection**, exfiltrate data through malicious business logic, or impact other processors sharing the same database. The stated mitigations: database isolation per project, **migrations validated and signed before execution**, input sanitisation of document operations, and audit logging of database operations.\n\n**Database access compromise.** Unauthorised access could expose all processed document data, modify processor-generated data, or disrupt operations. Mitigations: TLS on all connections, access restricted to processor instances, sensitive data encrypted at rest, encrypted and access-controlled backups.\n\nTwo of these are worth flagging as *aspirations rather than observed behaviour* \u2014 signed migrations and complete audit trails are listed as measures in a spec whose API description is otherwise out of date, so a reader should verify before relying on either. What is structurally true and independent of the spec's age: a processor runs inside the trust boundary, sees unfiltered operations, and shares a database with its siblings, so \"principle of least privilege\" for a processor means limiting which **tables** it touches \u2014 the namespace \u2014 not which documents it sees.\n\n## Provenance\n- `docs/specs/relational-db-processor.md` \u2014 Security \u203a Worst Case Scenarios, Data Protection, Security Measures\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:29:45.691Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:29:45.691Z"
    }
  },
  {
